    "result_text": "The build is green. There's exactly one test class in the suite, and it passed.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the level-4 tenure rule in the membership-level computation.\n\n**What was there before:** `membershipLevel` was an inline MapStruct expression in `OwnerMapper.java` that hard-capped at 3 via `Math.min(3, ...)` and only considered email presence and `namesakeCount`. Tenure and level 4 existed only in the OpenAPI docs/spec (\"Level 4 is reserved for tenure\") \u2014 there was no code computing it.\n\n**The change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`):\n- Extracted the logic into a `membershipLevel(Owner owner)` default method (mirroring the existing `ageBand` helper pattern), referenced from the `@Mapping` expression.\n- Added a tenure factor: `+1` when `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, today) > 365`.\n- Raised the cap from `Math.min(3, ...)` to `Math.min(4, ...)` so level 4 is now reachable \u2014 but **only** via tenure.\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is today, its tenure is 0 days, which is not `> 365`, so the tenure factor never fires on creation. A new owner with an email and `namesakeCount == 0` maxes the two pre-tenure factors at level 3 and cannot reach 4 \u2014 exactly as the spec and the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test require.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
